<tr id="S4.T3.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T3.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" colspan="4"><sup id="S4.T3.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.T3.2.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">a</span></sup><span id="S4.T3.2.8.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Fisher’s exact. <sup id="S4.T3.2.8.1.2.1" class="ltx_sup">b</sup>Mann–Whitney <math id="S4.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inter-Rater Reliability (ICC).</span>
We estimated ICC(2,1) and ICC(2,<math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>) via linear mixed-effects models with crossed random intercepts for stimuli and participants, computed on raw ratings. Presentation order and trial position were included as fixed-effect covariates. 95% CIs were obtained from 2,000 bootstrap resamples of stimuli. To test for modality differences, we pooled participants from both conditions and randomly reassigned them to pseudo-Audio and pseudo-Text groups (2,000 permutations), preserving original sample sizes. ICC values were numerically higher for audio (ICC(2,1) = .333 vs. .295; ICC(2,<math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>) = .821 vs. .788) but differences were not statistically significant (<math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=.127" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>.127</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=.127</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=.113" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>.113</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=.113</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively).</p>
</div>
